	<TR><TD bgcolor="#000000" valign="midle" align="center" style="padding:5"><B>Usage / Informations</B></TD></TR>
	<TR><TD><TABLE width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="2" border="0" style="font-family:verdana,sansserif;font-size:8pt"><TR><TD bgcolor="#D0D0D0" >
		To <B>add</B> you on the list enter your informations and hit submit. Make sure the Function is set to &quot;Add/View&quot;.<BR><BR>
		To only <B>view</B> your submitted informations just enter your name and password, set the function to &quot;Add/View&quot; and hit submit<BR><BR>
		If you want to <B>update</B> your informations you should enter your name and your password only. Than while the functions shows &quot;Add/View&quot;
		hit submit and your actual informations are loaded into the submit form. Now make your chances and set the function to &quot;Update&quot; if
		you want the changes to be done.<BR><BR>
		To <B>delete</B> yourself from the list enter your name and your password and set the function to &quot;Delete from list&quot; and hit submit.<BR><BR>
		If your name apears in <SPAN style="color:red">red</SPAN> than some informations you submitted are not correct. To be listed as a correct
		signup you need to set your class, your level has to be 47 or above and you need to have submitted a valid email address. If you did all those
		but your name is still red contact one of the officers of LSoG to make sure you are correct on the list.<BR><BR>
		Only correctly submitted persons can join the raid at the end. However if some informations are not provided it is up to the raid leader if
		he/she thinks you know all to join the raid.
		The list is allways sorted in the manner that members (M) are first in the list coz they have the best chance to come into the raid even if the
		maximum player limit is reached there is still a chance to join the raid. However it is not a garantee if you are beyond the maximum that you can
		come. Make sure to be ready if you want to come. You will be notified shortly before the raid starts.<BR><BR>
		The second on the list is allways the invited (I) guests. Those are people directly invited by someone in the guild. However make sure one of the
		Leaders / Officers invited you coz if not it is not very certain you can come. Invited guests has to submit the person who invited them and
		have allmost the same chance to join the raid like members (only in a very bad situation they may can't join).<BR><BR>
		The last on the list are the uninvited (U) guests. Since they are not direclty invited to come to the raid it is not very certain they can go.
		But it is maybe possible and depends on the number of members / invited people on the list as well as if the person is known to the guild.
	</TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR>

